{
  "tema": 7013,
  "slug": "que-preguntas-indirectas",
  "titulo": "Using qué in indirect questions",
  "subtitulo": "No sé qué carro comprar. Me pregunto qué va a pasar.",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "In indirect questions (no sé, dime, me pregunto...), qué keeps its accent. Qué + noun = which / what + noun, and never changes: no sé qué zapatos ponerme. Qué can also be followed by a verb or an infinitive.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "An **indirect question** is a question inside another sentence, after verbs like **saber**, **decir**, **preguntar(se)**, **decidir**, **no entender**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Qué** keeps its **accent** there, even without question marks."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "qué + noun",
              "texto": "_which / what + noun_: **no sé qué carro comprar**. **Qué** never changes, whatever the gender or number of the noun."
            },
            {
              "forma": "qué + verb",
              "texto": "_what_: **me pregunto qué va a pasar**."
            },
            {
              "forma": "qué + infinitive",
              "texto": "_what to_: **no sé qué ponerme**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: inside or outside question marks, a question is still a question, so **qué** keeps its hat."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sustantivo",
      "titulo": "Qué + noun",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "No sé ==qué carro== voy a comprar.",
              "en": "I don't know which car I'm going to buy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Dime ==qué casa== te gusta más.",
              "en": "Tell me which house you like best."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tienes que decidir ==qué vestidos== vas a donar.",
              "en": "You have to decide which dresses you're going to donate."
            },
            {
              "es": "No saben ==qué faldas== son las más baratas.",
              "en": "They don't know which skirts are the cheapest."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "verbo",
      "titulo": "Qué + verb or infinitive",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Todavía no decido ==qué== ponerme para la fiesta de Verónica.",
              "en": "I still haven't decided what to wear to Verónica's party."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me pregunto ==qué== va a pasar con Miguel ahora.",
              "en": "I wonder what's going to happen with Miguel now."
            },
            {
              "es": "No entiendo ==qué== quieres decir.",
              "en": "I don't understand what you mean."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
